.SH "NAME"
fexe \- print a process or corefile\*(Aqs executable path
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP \w'\fBfexe\fR\ 'u
\fBfexe\fR [\fIoptions\fR] {\fIprogram\fR\ \fIarg\fR\ ...  | \fIpid\fR... | \fIcore\-file\fR\ [\ \fIcore\-executable\fR\ ]... }
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBfexe\fR
prints a processe or corefile\*(Aqs full executable path to standard output\&.
.PP
\-v
.RS 4
Use more verbose output, the process, executable, and /proc/PID/exe contents are displayed\&.
.RE
.SS "Standard Frysk Options"
.PP
\fB\-exe\fR
.RS 4
The full path of the executable to read\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-noexe\fR
.RS 4
Do not attempt to read the corresponding executable when loading a core file\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-sysroot \fR\fB\fIdirectory\fR\fR
.RS 4
The system root directory under which all executables, libraries, and source are located\&.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-debug \fR\fB\fIclass\fR\fR\fB=\fR\fB\fIlevel\fR\fR\fB\&.\&.\&.\fR
.RS 4
Set internal debug\-tracing of the specified Java
\fIclass\fR
to
\fIlevel\fR
(level can be NONE, INFO, WARNING, FINE, and FINEST)\&. If the
\fIlevel\fR
is absent, FINE is assumed; if the
\fIclass\fR
is absent, the global level is set\&.
.RE
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.PP
In this sequence a copy of bash is created and then executed, the running processes path examined:
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
$ cp /bin/bash /tmp/sh
$ PS1=\*(Aqsh$ \*(Aq /tmp/sh
sh$ fexe $$
/tmp/sh
sh$ rm /tmp/sh
sh$ fexe \-v $$
1234 null /tmp/sh (deleted)
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
